    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d185">

                <pb facs="0164" n="160" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg160"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.30 Asiatic Fleet/468: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The First Secretary of Embassy in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Salisbury</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-07-27T09:00:00+08:00">July 27, 1938—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 27—4 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>466. [Following to Chefoo:] Your July 25, 2 p.m., has been repeated to Tokyo.
                    Embassy is pleased that both incidents are settled but notes that 5 days elapsed
                    between the occurrence of first incident and your reporting thereon and that
                    without obtaining instructions you took formal action involving acceptance of
                    conditions in the first incident including formal expression of regrets by you
                    as American Consul. In this particular connection, the Embassy is of the opinion
                    that expression of the regrets of Admiral Yarnell, if authorized by him, would
                    more appropriately have been made by an American naval officer.</p>
                <pb facs="0165" n="161" xml:id="pg161"/>
                <list>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Please report fully concerning both incidents including information as to
                        whether the terms of settlement of the first incident, which appear to
                        involve commitments by the United States Navy, were authorized by Admiral
                        Yarnell.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Sent to Chefoo; repeated to Hankow, Tokyo.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Salisbury</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
